# Terminal safety — forbidden commands

For any agent working in this repo (worktree implementer, reviewer, orchestrator):

**Never run** (stop and report if a task seems to require one — do not bypass):

- `git push --force` / `git push -f`
- `git commit --amend`
- `git commit --no-verify` / `git commit --no-gpg-sign`
- `git add -A` / `git add .` / `git add --all`
- `rm -rf` or broad `rm` on project paths
- `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, destructive `git checkout --`

**Prefer** explicit-path `git add <path>` only. Never commit to `main` —
work on `agent/<lineage>/<task>` and ship via PR (AGENTS.md → Workflow).

Project deny rules also live in `.cursor/cli.json` (`permissions.deny`). Cursor
IDE has no separate terminal deny-list UI — use allowlist mode plus these denies
and **Settings → Cursor Settings → Agents → Protection** (File-Deletion
Protection on).
